=2 Walkthrough
>The Boyahda Tree
!The Boyahda Tree-map1.jpg||Map 1
* Speak to {n:Tosuka-Porika} again for a cutscene. Zoning is not required after the previous mission.
* Speak to {n:Kohlo-Lakolo} in {z:Port Windurst} (G-5) (HP #1) behind Warehouse 1 for a cutscene.
** **(Optional)**: Talking to {n:Kohlo-Lakolo} again will give you a hint.
** **(Optional)**: Speaking to {n:Shanruru} gives an additional cutscene.
* Open up your Temporary Key Item menu and examine the {@k} {k:Piece of evidence} in your Temporary Key Items to see a cipher.
* Speak to {n:Kohlo-Lakolo} for another cutscene. He will ask if you deciphered the evidence, say __yup__.
** Even though you probably didn't, it seems your character did.
*** For anyone curious, the encrypted message uses a simple caesar cipher and says: "__I require the special egg and a very strong individual. First comes the egg.__"
* Travel to the {z:The Boyahda Tree} and visit any of the three **Muggy Air** sites at (D-5), (H-6), and (H-9) Map 1, bottom floor.
** The best option is to take the {p:Proto-Waypoint} to {z:The Boyahda Tree}, which places you on Map 1 in (D-4).
** You may instead take the {p:Unity Warp} (Level 125) to {z:The Boyahda Tree}. Once there, turn around to zone to Map 1.
** May need to travel to all 3 spots as one activates the cutscene.
* Touching the active site will immediately spawn the Templar Crawler NM. The active site will have a white glowing animation.{br}Not all sites will be active, so keep looking at the different positions.
** Deals enhanced damage via **Poison Breath**.
** Appears to gain an additional {p:Protect} buff after using **Cocoon**.
* Each party member will receive a {@k} {k:Sublime lucky egg} upon defeating the NM.
* Return to {n:Kohlo-Lakolo} for a cutscene and your reward.

